Design and implement a provider-agnostic AI metering and cost tracking layer for a ChatGPT-like application with frontend and backend.

Current provider is OpenAI using the OpenAI SDK, but the architecture must be extensible to Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, Mistral, local models, embeddings, image generation, audio transcription, OCR, vector database calls, web search tools, and future AI providers.

Requirements:

1. Introduce an AI Gateway / LLM Router layer so the application never calls the OpenAI SDK directly from business logic.
2. Create provider adapters:
   - OpenAIAdapter initially
   - interface ready for AnthropicAdapter, GeminiAdapter, LocalModelAdapter
3. Implement Usage Metering:
   - capture estimated input usage before the request when possible
   - capture actual usage after provider response
   - store usage by tenant_id, user_id, case_id, chat_id, message_id, provider, model, request_id
4. Implement a generic UsageUnit abstraction:
   - unit_type: input_tokens, output_tokens, cached_input_tokens, reasoning_tokens, image_tokens, audio_seconds, ocr_pages, tool_calls, vector_db_reads, embedding_tokens, etc.
   - quantity
   - billable_quantity
   - metadata
5. Implement Pricing Engine:
   - prices configurable in database or JSON
   - support provider, model, unit_type, price_per_unit, currency, valid_from, valid_to
   - calculate estimated cost and final cost
   - support cached tokens, discounted tokens, free quota, custom tenant markup
6. Persist:
   - AIRequest
   - AIUsageEvent
   - AICostEvent
   - AIModelPricing
   - optional Budget records per user, tenant, case and project
7. Add budget controls:
   - warn when estimated request cost exceeds threshold
   - block when user/case/tenant monthly budget is exceeded
   - expose usage summaries to frontend
8. Add API endpoints:
   - GET /ai/usage/chat/{chat_id}
   - GET /ai/usage/case/{case_id}
   - GET /ai/usage/user/{user_id}
   - GET /ai/usage/tenant/{tenant_id}
   - GET /ai/pricing/models
9. Frontend:
   - show estimated cost before sending, when available
   - show actual cost after response
   - show total cost by chat/case
   - show token breakdown
10. Engineering constraints:
   - clean separation of concerns
   - no provider-specific logic in frontend
   - no OpenAI-specific usage model leaking into business logic
   - fully typed DTOs/interfaces
   - unit tests for pricing engine and adapters
   - integration test with mocked OpenAI response
   - migration scripts for database schema

Deliver:
- Proposed folder structure
- Database schema/migrations
- Type/interface definitions
- OpenAIAdapter implementation
- PricingEngine implementation
- UsageMeteringService implementation
- API endpoints
- Frontend usage/cost display components
- Tests
